Convert file names to uppercase
- `#!/bin/bash` – Runs the script using Bash.
- `for file in "$@"` – Takes all file names given as command-line arguments one by one.
- `do` – Starts the loop.
- `newname=$(echo "$file" | tr 'a-z' 'A-Z')` – Converts the file name from lowercase to uppercase and stores it in `newname`.
- `tr 'a-z' 'A-Z'` – Converts lowercase letters into uppercase.
- `mv "$file" "$newname"` – Renames the original file with the new uppercase name.
- `echo "Renamed to $newname"` – Displays the new file name.
- `done` – Ends the loop.

